is a terminal tile that doesn't combine well with my other tiles, and keeping the W6,W7,W8 sequence offers more flexibility to form a chow with one draw (either W5 or W9). Also, B1 might be less likely to be useful for other players since one meld of B1,B2,B3 is already exposed, reducing the chance of someone needing B1 for a pung or chow.  \n\nAnswer: Play B1"}
