ul and has low chance to pair. Also, discarding B1 might be safe: looking at history, B1 has been played once by me earlier (my history: Play B1), and the player across has a Chow B1B2B3, so they used a B1. That means there are fewer B1 left, but also others might not need it. However, B1 is a terminal, so some may avoid it, but it's not extremely dangerous. W6, W7, W8 are middle tiles, more dangerous because they can be used in many sequences. But I need them. So among W6, W7, W8, which to discard if I must? Actually, my valid actions are Play W6, Play W7, Play B1, Play W8. I should choose Play B1. But let's check if there's a reason to keep B1 for some pattern? Possibly for All Types? I already have suits: B (from B5 pung and maybe B1), T (from chows), W (from hand), and honors? I have no honors yet. So All Types requires all three suits and winds and dragons. I don't have winds or dragons, so not close. B1 is a terminal, which could help with Pung of Terminals or Honors, but unlikely. So discard B1.\n\nReason: I have a pair of W7 and potential to form a Chow with W6-W7-W8. Discarding B1 preserves my chances to complete a Chow by drawing W5 or W9, and also keeps the possibility of drawing another W6 or W8 to form a pung. B1 is a lone tile with only one copy left, making it unlikely to become useful. Also, discarding B1 is relatively safe given it's a terminal and has been played before.\n\nAnswer: Play B1"}
